## When to Use Each Mode

### Decision Matrix

| Situation | Recommended Mode | Why |
|-----------|-----------------|-----|
| "How does this function work?" | Ask | Just need explanation |
| "What does this error mean?" | Ask | Debugging information |
| "Refactor this module" | Agent | Needs code changes |
| "Fix this bug" | Agent | Needs code changes |
| "Add a new feature" | Plan → Agent | Analyze first, then implement |
| "Should I use Redux or Zustand?" | Plan | Needs analysis and options |
| "Review this PR" | Plan | Analysis + recommendations |
| "Compare three approaches" | Plan | Presents options |
| "Migrate to TypeScript 5" | Plan → Agent | Analyze first, execute after |
| "What's the complexity of this function?" | Ask | Understanding only |
| "Write unit tests for this" | Agent | Needs file creation |
| "Optimize this query" | Plan → Agent | Analyze, then implement |

### Mode Selection Flow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[New task] --> B{Do you want changes made?}
    B -->|No, just info| C[Ask Mode]
    B -->|Yes| D{Do you want analysis first?}
    D -->|Yes, present options| E[Plan Mode]
    D -->|No, just do it| F[Agent Mode]
    
    E --> G{Agent recommends approach?}
    G -->|User approves| H[Switch to Agent Mode]
    G -->|User decides| I[Agent implements chosen approach]
    
    C --> J[Agent explains]
    F --> K[Agent acts]
    H --> K
    I --> K
```

