## Mode-Specific Tool Access

### Tools Available Per Mode

| Tool | Ask | Plan | Agent | Notes |
|------|-----|------|-------|-------|
| `Read` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | All modes |
| `Write` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Write/create files |
| `StrReplace` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | In-place edit |
| `EditNotebook` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Edit Jupyter cells |
| `Delete` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Delete file |
| `Grep` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | All modes |
| `Glob` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | All modes |
| `SemanticSearch` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | All modes |
| `WebSearch` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | All modes |
| `WebFetch` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | All modes |
| `Shell` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Execute commands |
| `Task` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Spawn subagent |
| `CallMcpTool` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | MCP tools |
| `TodoWrite` | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ | Manage tasks |
| `ReadLints` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | All modes |
| `StrReplace` (dry-run) | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | Plan can propose |
| `Write` (dry-run) | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ | Plan can propose |

### Plan Mode Projections

Plan Mode can "propose" changes without executing them:

```
Agent (Plan Mode):
"Here's my plan for adding rate limiting:

1. Modify src/api/server.ts:
   - Add express-rate-limit import
   - Create rateLimit config object
   - Apply middleware to /api routes
   
2. Create tests/test-rate-limit.ts:
   - Test 1: Request within limit
   - Test 2: Request exceeding limit
   - Test 3: Custom error response
   
[Proposed changes are shown but NOT applied]
"
```

The user can then:
- Switch to Agent Mode to apply
- Request modifications to the plan
- Reject the plan entirely

